// Where an empty list literal is allowed. idc.py hands an expected type down
// one level, from four places only: a typed declaration, an assignment to a
// known variable, the value of an index-assignment, and push's second
// argument. The AST has no parent links, so the same question is asked
// backwards -- does any node hand THIS node a list type?
//
// That is answered once for the whole store, not once per literal: arrmark
// holds a 1 for every node some other node hands a list type, built by one
// pass over the store the first time a literal asks. A scan per literal looked
// affordable while empty literals were rare; with hundreds of them it was
// literals x nodes, and the type check's cold run spent four fifths of its
// time in it.

arr_ok(int id) {
  if(len((import arrmark)) != len((import nkind))) {
    arr_marks();
  }
  int ok = (import arrmark)[id];
} return int ok;
